    "how_to_read": [
      "`evaluation.scores.events` is class-strict: an alarm is a hit only when the predict track *named* the class that occurred. A district correctly flagged under a different class therefore appears there as a false alarm, which is why the class-agnostic `detection.flagged_any_class` exists \u2014 read them together.",
      "`evaluation.scores.per_class` is one-vs-rest per class. `pod: 0.0` with `misses: N` for the episode class means the track never named that class, not that it scored the district low; `detection.episode_class_over_threshold` separates the two.",
      "`detection` counts over the districts the sources name, per horizon.",
      "Nothing in this report covers a district nobody named. Unknown is not clear, and the far column is unmeasurable rather than zero when no negative sample exists."
    ],
